mypy/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/deployments","created_at":"2012-12-07T13:30:23Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T11:48:01Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-11T20:11:30Z","git_url":"git://github.com/python/mypy.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:python/mypy.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy","homepage":"https://www.mypy-lang.org/","size":77161,"stargazers_count":20064,"watchers_count":20064,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":3065,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":3124,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["linter","python","typechecker","types","typing"],"visibility":"public","forks":3065,"open_issues":3124,"watchers":20064,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/pulls/3952","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/3952","diff_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/3952.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/3952.patch","merged_at":"2017-09-27T17:58:45Z"},"body":"Fixes https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/3340\r\nFixes https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/3419\r\nFixes https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/3674\r\nFixes https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/3685\r\nFixes https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/3799\r\nFixes https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/3836\r\nFixes https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/3881\r\nFixes https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/867\r\nFixes https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/2241\r\nFixes https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/2399\r\nFixes https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/1701\r\nFixes https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/3016\r\nFixes https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/3054\r\nFixes https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/2762\r\nFixes https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/3575\r\nFixes https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/3990\r\n\r\nCurrently, forward references don't work with anything apart from classes, for example this doesn't work:\r\n```python\r\nx: A\r\nA = NamedTuple('A', [('x', int)])\r\n```\r\nThe same situation is with ``TypedDict``s, ``NewType``s, and type aliases. The root problem is that these synthetic types are neither detected in first pass, nor fixed in third pass. In certain cases this can lead to _crashes_ (first six issues above are various crash scenarios). I fix these crashes by applying some additional patches after third pass. Here is the summary of the PR:\r\n* New simple wrapper type ``ForwardRef`` with only one field ``link`` is introduced (with updates to type visitors)\r\n* When an unknown type is found in second pass, the corresponding ``UnboundType`` is wrapped in ``ForwardRef``, it is given a \"second chance\" in third pass.\r\n* After third pass I record the \"suspicious\" nodes, where forward references and synthetic types have been encountered and append patches (callbacks) to fix them after third pass. Patches use the new visitor ``TypeReplacer`` (which is the core of this PR).\r\n\r\nHere are two problems that I encountered:\r\n* Third pass (both in ``semanal.py`` and in ``typeanal.py``) was more \"shallow\" than the second one, some visitor methods were literally ``pass``. It was necessary to update these to match the \"depth\" of the second pass.\r\n* Now third pass has a link to second pass analyzer, ``self.sem``, same as for first pass. It would be nice to refactor the passes since all three share some code/functionality, there is already https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/3459 to track this.\r\n\r\nNOTE:  self-referential types are still _not_ properly supported, but now we give a reasonable error for this, not a crash, and they still can be used to certain extent, for example:\r\n```python\r\nclass MyNamedTuple(NamedTuple):\r\n    parent: 'MyNamedTuple'\r\n\r\ndef get_parent(nt: MyNamedTuple) -> MyNamedTuple:\r\n    return nt.parent\r\n\r\nx: MyNamedTuple\r\nreveal_type(x.parent)\r\nreveal_type(x[0])\r\n```\r\nresults in\r\n```\r\nmain:2: error: Recursive types not fully supported yet, nested types replaced with \"Any\"\r\nmain:9: error: Revealed type is 'Tuple[Any, fallback=__main__.MyNamedTuple]\r\nmain:10: error: Revealed type is 'Tuple[Any, fallback=__main__.MyNamedTuple]\r\n```\r\nProper support of recursive types would be much harder (mostly due to (de-)serialization that would require something similar to ``type_ref``), there is a separate issue for this https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/731.\r\n\r\n@JukkaL sorry it took a bit longer than expected because of CPython sprint last week.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/3952/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/3952/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":1268308598,"node_id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTI2ODMwODU5OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/events/1268308598","actor":{"login":"JukkaL","id":1107911,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDc5MTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1107911?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JukkaL","html_url":"https://github.com/JukkaL","followers_url":"https:/